/-!
# Stage-9A full mother connection descent and analytic transport

This module closes the remaining S9-A provenance seam.  The smooth affine
extension of the actual Stage-8 mother connection is shifted chartwise by the
same source-generated hypercharge transition used to glue the total bundle.
Because that transition commutes with every P286-block value generated by the
Stage-8 source, the full connection satisfies the complete adjoint plus
inhomogeneous overlap law.  Reusing the unshifted global potential in every
chart is rejected by the nonzero transition derivative.

Along every coordinate-axis segment, antisymmetry makes the contracted full
mother potential constant.  Its matrix exponential is therefore an explicit
analytic parallel-transport solution.  Lean proves its derivative equation,
zero and composition laws, and exact recovery of the Stage-8 potential as the
transport derivative at zero.  The positive source has two noncommuting axis
generators and a nonconstant transport, so this is not an Abelian trace
surrogate.  No ODE solution, bundle, connection, or descent certificate is a
source field.
-/

